## How to differentiate *plain place-name* layers from shields

| Property | Place-name layer (typical) | Shield layer (typical) |
|----------|---------------------------|------------------------|
| `icon-image` | *either absent* or a generic POI icon (`"city"` / `"town"` / `"place"`). | Contains `{network}_{ref_length}` or `road_{ref_length}` (or `default_{ref_length}`). |
| `text-field` | Usually `"{name}"` or `["get","name"]`. | `"{ref}"` or `["get","ref"]`. |
| `icon-text-fit` | **Absent** (or `"none"`). | `"both"` / `"width"` (stretchable) **or** absent (pre-drawn badge). |
| `icon-size` | Often varies per zoom, but not tied to `ref_length`. | May be constant or scaled with `["interpolate",["linear"],["zoom"],... ]`. |
| `icon-allow-overlap` | Usually `false` (labels collide). | Often `true` (shields should stay visible). |
| `symbol-placement` | `"point"` (or omitted → default `"point"`). | `"point"` **or** an expression/zoom-function that also yields `"line"` at higher zooms. |
| `text-anchor` | May be `"center"` or `"left"`/`"right"` depending on label placement. | Usually left undefined (defaults to `"center"`). **Not a discriminant**. |

Thus, **the decisive discriminants are `icon-image` and `text-field`**. If you need a quick “yes/no” you can stop after those two checks; add the optional `icon-text-fit` test if you want to be extra sure.

